A pause keeps the position the remote was showing.

Spirc reports a pause twice: handle_pause sends the position its own
clock had reached, which is the one every remote was extrapolating, and
the player's Paused event then overwrites it with the player's stream
position. That position is ahead of the first by everything the backend
has taken and not yet played, which with a pipe backend feeding another
player is half a second or more, so every pause stepped the phone's
slider forward a moment after it showed the pause. The supervisor
behind the pipe then seeks back to where the sound actually stopped,
which is a step the other way; the forward one in between was noise.

Now a Paused event for a pause Spirc itself made keeps the position it
already reported. A pause the player made on its own, with Spirc still
Playing, still takes the player's position, since that is the only one
there is.

Applies on top of librespot-control-socket.patch,
librespot-session-loss-reconnect.patch and
librespot-play-from-stopped.patch.

--- a/connect/src/spirc.rs	2026-09-08 11:14:40
+++ b/connect/src/spirc.rs	2026-09-08 11:14:40
@@ -774,7 +774,19 @@
             } => {
                 trace!("==> Paused");
                 match self.play_status {
-                    SpircPlayStatus::Paused { .. } | SpircPlayStatus::Playing { .. } => {
+                    // The pause came through handle_pause, which already put
+                    // the position where the clock the remote shows had it.
+                    // The player's own position is ahead of that by whatever
+                    // the backend has taken and not yet played, so reporting
+                    // it here stepped the remote's slider forward on every
+                    // pause, a moment after it showed the pause.
+                    SpircPlayStatus::Paused { position_ms, .. } => {
+                        self.play_status = SpircPlayStatus::Paused {
+                            position_ms,
+                            preloading_of_next_track_triggered: false,
+                        };
+                    }
+                    SpircPlayStatus::Playing { .. } => {
                         self.connect_state
                             .update_position(new_position_ms, self.now_ms());
                         self.play_status = SpircPlayStatus::Paused {
